+## Assignment null and limitations
+
+The tree, posterior states, masks, rates and scan settings remain fixed. Size
+bins and branch eligibility are fixed independently of foreground labels. The
+original configuration is always allowed; lineage mode preserves each lineage’s
+component count in each bin. Size matching alone does not match branch lengths,
+phylogenetic depth, composition, missingness or reconstruction uncertainty.
+
+Small spaces are enumerated. Larger spaces use uniform complete allocations
+and reject the whole allocation if clades overlap, rather than sampling clades
+sequentially from changing pools. Complete enumeration uses the exact tail
+fraction. Monte Carlo uses `(1 + extreme_count) / (B + 1)` with replacement,
+including ties and repeated configurations.
+
+The former `--scan_permutation_sample_original no` and
+`--scan_permutation_retry_sample_original yes` settings are rejected when
+calibration is enabled. Defaults are now `yes` and `no`, respectively. A failed
+or undefined trial makes calibration unavailable: the null is not restricted
+to successful trials. A successful full-scan trial without candidates contributes
+1. Diagnostics are saved separately even when the observed scan has no rows.
+
+`full_scan` covers candidate discovery across the sites and match classes in one
+single-trait run. It does not cover multiple genes, repeated parameter choices,
+or automatically guarantee strong FWER control under mixed null/signal sites.
+Multi-trait listing is supported with calibration disabled; calibrated
+multi-trait scans require a joint assignment model and are currently rejected.
+For an observational foreground, the assignment-null assumption needs scientific
+justification. Sequence generation, fitting and ASR must be included in any
+claim about calibration of the biological analysis pipeline.
+
+See the [complete calibration contract](https://github.com/kfuku52/csubst/blob/master/docs/SCAN_CALIBRATION.md)
+for the sampler, diagnostic schema and verification boundary.
+
